sequenceDiagram
  %% status: draft
  %% command: proof:pool:resume
  %% kind: proof.pool.resume
  autonumber
  participant CLI as Operator<br/>CLI · MCP
  participant GW as Gateway
  participant SW as Swamp
  participant CP as CI Nodes<br/>warm copies
  CLI->>GW: Resume the warm pool
  GW->>GW: Clear the drain
  %%> A pool that is not drained stays as it is: the command changes nothing.
  GW->>GW: Refill the warm pool
  %%> Start warm copies until the pool holds proof.warm_copies, on Nodes with a free place, the Nodes in turns. A refill never waits for a place: a Node without one gets its warm copy at a later refill.
  GW-->>CLI: Resumed<br/>warm copies being made
  SW->>CP: Create each warm copy<br/>from the Node's seed
  %%> The same instance.create as any proof copy: it holds its place and stops idle runners down to the Node's limit.
